<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29322" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύ̆σ-ορμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with bad anchorage</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆσος . . δ. ναυσί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					448
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δ.</span>
			<i>rough</i> ground, <i>where one can scarce get footing</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				10.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνοαὶ δ.</span>
			<i>that detained</i> the fleet <i>in harbour</i> or <i>that
				kept</i> it <i>from reaching harbour, foul</i> winds, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				193
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
